Themes, keybindings, preview/cancel state, cursor style, image-render preferences, Mermaid display options and other pure appearance/interaction state belong in src/ava/tui, app/tui or tui-named files, tui-thread-only without locks/UnlockedData. Do not create canonical theme, keybinding, preview or draft domains. Draft text remains frontend-only until submitted as a string. Classify ambiguous settings by actual effect: model variant/reasoning affecting execution is backend state, reasoning display is UI-only; attachment authority is backend-owned, image visibility/rendering is local. Keep external service capabilities separate from local preferences and backend authority. Preserve approved settings persistence, precedence and actionable reload failures without making persistence alone a reason for UnlockedData.

